Employee demography means the demographic characteristics or basic information about employees in an organization.
It can include:

Age – e.g., 20–30, 31–40 years
Gender – male, female, etc.
Education – degree, BTech, MBA, etc.
Marital status
Work experience
Job position/designation
Department
Salary range
Location
Years of service
Simple example
If a company has 100 employees, employee demography might show:
Category	Example
Age	Most employees are 21–35
Gender	60% male, 40% female
Education	70% graduates
Experience	Average 3 years
Department	IT, HR, Finance, Sales
In simple words: Employee demography = “What kind of people make up the company's workforce?”

